WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Madinah, in the Prophet's lifetime.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.200
Some Muslim parents have
sons who were raised as Jews.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.500
They want to force them into Islam.

4
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:12.820
A verse forbids it: let there
be no compulsion in religion.

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.110
Yet classical law set a
penalty for leaving Islam,

6
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.280
and in a few states today
courts may apply it.

7
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.080
So if there is no compulsion in religion,

8
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.970
why do some laws punish leaving Islam?

9
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.950
In this mission, you'll trace the ruling
on leaving Islam from the Qur'an and

10
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.030
hadith to courts today.

11
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.080
Then you'll weigh what
freedom of belief should mean:

12
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.670
to hold, to practise,
or to change a belief.

13
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.340
Your mission: find out why Muslims
answer this question so differently,

14
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.730
and weigh their reasons.
